# CAGED: One Melody Everywhere (repertoire plan: st-caged-melody). An original 8-bar tune in
# C major, played five times at the same pitch, once in each CAGED position of the guitar engine,
# climbing the neck: C shape (open), A shape (2nd position), G shape (5th), E shape (7th) and
# D shape (10th). The tune stays between G3 and G4, the range every position holds, so only the
# frets and fingers change, never the notes.
# The teacher strums the C chord in the matching shape from the CAGED chord study:
#   C (x32010), A-shape C (x35553), G-shape C (875558), E-shape C (8-10-10-9-8-8),
#   D-shape C (x-x-10-12-13-12).
# The tune: E G E D C | E D C A G | C E G F E | D E D | E G E D C | E D C A G A B | C E G F E D | C.
# Over the one chord, every note on beats 1 and 3 is C, E or G, or a step to one of them.
title: CAGED: One Melody Everywhere
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the CAGED positions of C major
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 7
tags: caged, positions, melody, whole neck
tempo: 96
time: 4/4
key: C

